// autolod: three generated subjects (a maple, a rock and a house), each turned into
// levels of detail and an octahedral impostor by 'autoLod', and shown from close to
// two kilometres, headless: no window, a 1920 x 1080 sRGB target, GPU timestamps.
//
//   congo run --release packages/autolod/examples/autolod.cone -- --report
//   congo run --release packages/autolod/examples/autolod.cone -- --shots <folder>
//   congo run --release packages/autolod/examples/autolod.cone -- --bench
//
// GPU_POWER_PREFERENCE=low-power runs it on the integrated GPU where there are two.
// With the Vulkan SDK, validation is on and must say nothing.
//
// --report   what the levels are: for each subject and part, the triangles, the thresholds
//            (pixels across the object), the error budget each level was made to and the
//            largest distance it measures from level 0, and the impostor's atlas size and
//            how long the levels and the bake took.
// --shots    for each subject: at each switch size (where one level hands over to the next)
//            two pictures, a little above the size (the finer level) and a little below
//            (the coarser), each drawn with that level alone, with the difference between
//            them, and numbers for the pop (the share of the subject's pixels that change by
//            more than 24 of 255, and the mean change); then the subject through the scene
//            at 10, 30, 100, 300, 1000 and 2000 metres, levels chosen by size, cross-faded.
//            Crops of the 1920 x 1080 frame about the subject, as .bmp.
// --bench    a forest, a rock field and a village of the three subjects over 4 km by 4 km,
//            drawn from the ground to 2.4 km, with the levels off (every copy at level 0), the
//            mesh levels alone, and the mesh levels with the impostor: the GPU and CPU time of a
//            frame and the triangles drawn.

mod autolodexample;

import stdio use *;
import libc;
import sdl;
import geomath use *;
import collections use *;
import mesh use Mesh;
import gpu use *;
import render use *;
import autolod use *;
import weberpenn use *;
import noiserock use *;
import path as filepath;

const W = 1920u32;
const H = 1080u32;

// ---- Subjects ----

fn boxAt(center Vec3, half Vec3) Mesh {
  var m = Mesh.cube(1.);
  m.transform(Mat4.fromTrs(center, Quat.identity(), half));
  m
}

// A maple: its trunk and its crown, two parts
fn mapleParts(seed u32, height f32) List[BakePart] {
  let params = redMaple(seed, height);
  let tree = grow(&params);
  let tube = new TubeParams();
  let trunk = branchMesh(&tree, &tube);
  var leaf = mapleFoliage(seed + 100u32);
  leaf.leafSize = 0.17;
  leaf.detail = 7;
  let crown = foliageMesh(&tree, &leaf);
  var parts = List[BakePart].empty();
  parts.push(new BakePart(trunk, Material.plain(new Color(0.20, 0.12, 0.07, 1.)), Image.empty()));
  parts.push(new BakePart(crown, Material.plain(new Color(0.10, 0.28, 0.05, 1.)), Image.empty(), true));
  parts
}

fn rockParts(seed u32) List[BakePart] {
  var p = new RockParams();
  p.seed = seed;
  p.width = 1.6;
  p.height = 1.1;
  p.depth = 1.3;
  p.rings = 16;
  p.slices = 28;
  p.facets = 9;
  p.smooth = true;
  let rock = rockMesh(&p);
  var parts = List[BakePart].empty();
  parts.push(new BakePart(rock, Material.plain(new Color(0.34, 0.33, 0.31, 1.)), Image.empty()));
  parts
}

// A window of frame bars and a pane at 'at', on the wall facing 'face' (+z or +x), 'w' wide
fn windowMeshes(frame &mut Mesh, glass &mut Mesh, at Vec3, alongX bool, w f32, h f32) {
  let t = 0.06;
  let d = 0.16;
  let hx = if alongX { w * 0.5 } else { d };
  let hz = if alongX { d } else { w * 0.5 };
  let tx = if alongX { t } else { d };
  let tz = if alongX { d } else { t };
  // the frame: left, right (along the wall), top, bottom, a cross bar each way
  if alongX {
    frame.append(&boxAt(at + new Vec3(-w * 0.5, 0., 0.), new Vec3(t, h * 0.5, d)));
    frame.append(&boxAt(at + new Vec3(w * 0.5, 0., 0.), new Vec3(t, h * 0.5, d)));
    frame.append(&boxAt(at + new Vec3(0., h * 0.5, 0.), new Vec3(hx, t, d)));
    frame.append(&boxAt(at + new Vec3(0., -h * 0.5, 0.), new Vec3(hx, t, d)));
    frame.append(&boxAt(at, new Vec3(t * 0.6, h * 0.5, d * 0.8)));
    frame.append(&boxAt(at + new Vec3(0., h * 0.1, 0.), new Vec3(hx, t * 0.6, d * 0.8)));
    glass.append(&boxAt(at, new Vec3(hx, h * 0.5, d * 0.4)));
  } else {
    frame.append(&boxAt(at + new Vec3(0., 0., -w * 0.5), new Vec3(d, h * 0.5, t)));
    frame.append(&boxAt(at + new Vec3(0., 0., w * 0.5), new Vec3(d, h * 0.5, t)));
    frame.append(&boxAt(at + new Vec3(0., h * 0.5, 0.), new Vec3(d, t, hz)));
    frame.append(&boxAt(at + new Vec3(0., -h * 0.5, 0.), new Vec3(d, t, hz)));
    frame.append(&boxAt(at, new Vec3(d * 0.8, h * 0.5, t * 0.6)));
    frame.append(&boxAt(at + new Vec3(0., h * 0.1, 0.), new Vec3(d * 0.8, t * 0.6, hz)));
    glass.append(&boxAt(at, new Vec3(d * 0.4, h * 0.5, hz)));
  }
}

// A house, 10 by 7 metres, two floors, a tiled gable roof, a chimney: four parts (walls, tiles, window
// frames, glass), about 8000 triangles
fn houseParts() List[BakePart] {
  var walls = boxAt(new Vec3(0., 3., 0.), new Vec3(5., 3., 3.5));
  walls.append(&boxAt(new Vec3(-2.6, 7.4, 0.6), new Vec3(0.4, 1.2, 0.4)));                // chimney
  walls.append(&boxAt(new Vec3(1.5, 1.1, 3.6), new Vec3(0.6, 1.1, 0.12)));                // door
  walls.append(&boxAt(new Vec3(1.5, 0.08, 4.0), new Vec3(1.1, 0.08, 0.5)));               // step
  var frames = Mesh.empty();
  var glass = Mesh.empty();
  var floor = 0;
  while floor < 2 {
    let y = 1.5 + f32.from(floor) * 3.;
    var k = 0;
    while k < 4 {
      let x = -3.6 + f32.from(k) * 2.4;
      if !(floor == 0 and k == 3) {
        windowMeshes(&mut frames, &mut glass, new Vec3(x, y, 3.5), true, 1.0, 1.4);
      }
      windowMeshes(&mut frames, &mut glass, new Vec3(x, y, -3.5), true, 1.0, 1.4);
      k = k + 1;
    }
    windowMeshes(&mut frames, &mut glass, new Vec3(5., y, -1.2), false, 1.0, 1.4);
    windowMeshes(&mut frames, &mut glass, new Vec3(5., y, 1.2), false, 1.0, 1.4);
    windowMeshes(&mut frames, &mut glass, new Vec3(-5., y, -1.2), false, 1.0, 1.4);
    windowMeshes(&mut frames, &mut glass, new Vec3(-5., y, 1.2), false, 1.0, 1.4);
    floor = floor + 1;
  }
  // the roof: each slope one connected sheet, a grid with the tiles as relief on it: 14 rows of overlapping
  // tiles up the slope (each row a ramp that steps down to the next), 22 tiles across, each a rounded
  // ridge; four grid cells to a row, four to a tile (a slope rises 3.2 m over 4 m of run)
  var tiles = Mesh.empty();
  let run = 4.0;
  let rise = 3.2;
  let length = (run * run + rise * rise).sqrt();
  let nx = 88;
  let ny = 56;
  var side = 0;
  while side < 2 {
    let sign = if side == 0 { 1. } else { -1. };
    let base = u32.from(tiles.positions.len());
    var j = 0;
    while j <= ny {
      var i = 0;
      while i <= nx {
        let u = f32.from(i) / f32.from(nx);
        let v = f32.from(j) / f32.from(ny);
        // the surface, then the relief along the slope's normal
        let rowPhase = v * 14. - libc.floorf(v * 14.);
        let tilePhase = u * 22.;
        let relief = 0.045 * (1. - rowPhase) + 0.02 * libc.sinf(tilePhase * 6.2831853);
        let along = v * length;
        let x = -5.3 + u * 10.6;
        let y = 6. + along * (rise / length) + relief * (run / length);
        let z = sign * (4.0 - along * (run / length) + relief * (rise / length));
        tiles.positions.push(new Vec3(x, y, z));
        tiles.uvs.push(new Vec2(u * 22., v * 14.));
        i = i + 1;
      }
      j = j + 1;
    }
    j = 0;
    while j < ny {
      var i = 0;
      while i < nx {
        let a = base + u32.from(j * (nx + 1) + i);
        let b = a + 1u32;
        let c = a + u32.from(nx + 1);
        let d = c + 1u32;
        // facing out of the roof: +y and away from the ridge
        if side == 0 {
          tiles.indices.push(a); tiles.indices.push(b); tiles.indices.push(c);
          tiles.indices.push(b); tiles.indices.push(d); tiles.indices.push(c);
        } else {
          tiles.indices.push(a); tiles.indices.push(c); tiles.indices.push(b);
          tiles.indices.push(b); tiles.indices.push(c); tiles.indices.push(d);
        }
        i = i + 1;
      }
      j = j + 1;
    }
    side = side + 1;
  }
  tiles.computeSmoothNormals();
  tiles.append(&boxAt(new Vec3(0., 9.25, 0.), new Vec3(5.4, 0.06, 0.12)));    // ridge cap
  // gable ends: triangles of wall under the roof
  var gable = Mesh.empty();
  var e = 0;
  while e < 2 {
    let x = if e == 0 { 4.95 } else { -4.95 };
    let nx = if e == 0 { 1. } else { -1. };
    let base = u32.from(gable.positions.len());
    gable.positions.push(new Vec3(x, 6., -3.5));
    gable.positions.push(new Vec3(x, 6., 3.5));
    gable.positions.push(new Vec3(x, 9.1, 0.));
    var n = 0;
    while n < 3 { gable.normals.push(new Vec3(nx, 0., 0.)); n = n + 1; }
    if e == 0 {
      gable.indices.push(base); gable.indices.push(base + 2u32); gable.indices.push(base + 1u32);
    } else {
      gable.indices.push(base); gable.indices.push(base + 1u32); gable.indices.push(base + 2u32);
    }
    e = e + 1;
  }
  walls.append(&gable);
  var parts = List[BakePart].empty();
  parts.push(new BakePart(walls, Material.plain(new Color(0.55, 0.46, 0.33, 1.)), Image.empty()));
  parts.push(new BakePart(tiles, Material.plain(new Color(0.40, 0.14, 0.08, 1.)), Image.empty()));
  parts.push(new BakePart(frames, Material.plain(new Color(0.70, 0.68, 0.62, 1.)), Image.empty()));
  parts.push(new BakePart(glass, Material.plain(new Color(0.03, 0.05, 0.08, 1.)), Image.empty()));
  parts
}

fn totalTriangles(parts &List[BakePart]) u32 {
  var n = 0u32;
  var p = 0usize;
  while p < parts.len() {
    n = n + u32.from(parts[p].mesh.triangleCount());
    p = p + 1usize;
  }
  n
}

fn seconds(from u64, to u64) f64 { f64.from(to - from) / f64.from(sdl.GetPerformanceFrequency()) }

fn cstrEquals(a *u8, b &str) bool {
  var i = 0usize;
  while i < b.len() {
    if *(a + i) != b[i] { return false; }
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  *(a + b.len()) == 0u8
}

// ---- The report ----

fn reportOne(name &str, parts &List[BakePart], lod &AutoLod, settings &AutoLodSettings) {
  printStr(name); print <- ": "; print <- u64.from(parts.len()); print <- " part(s), "; print <- u64.from(totalTriangles(parts));
  print <- " triangles at level 0; object radius "; print <- lod.radius; print <- " m, the impostor from "; print <- settings.lods.switchSize(settings.lods.levels - 1u32);
  print <- " px\n";
  var p = 0usize;
  while p < lod.sets.len() {
    print <- "  part "; print <- u64.from(p); print <- " (radius "; print <- lod.sets[p].radius; print <- " m";
    if p == lod.anchor { print <- ", carries the impostor"; }
    print <- ", "; print <- u64.from(lod.sets[p].degenerate); print <- " degenerate triangles dropped, "; print <- u64.from(lod.sets[p].refused); print <- " levels refused for saving too little):\n";
    var k = 0usize;
    while k < lod.sets[p].levels.len() {
      print <- "    level "; print <- u64.from(k); print <- ": "; print <- u64.from(lod.sets[p].levels[k].triangles); print <- " triangles, drawn from ";
      print <- lod.sets[p].levels[k].minSize; print <- " px, budget "; print <- lod.sets[p].levels[k].budget; print <- " m, quadric error ";
      print <- lod.sets[p].levels[k].error; print <- " m, measured "; print <- lod.sets[p].levels[k].measured; print <- " m\n";
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    p = p + 1usize;
  }
  if lod.hasImpostor {
    print <- "  impostor: "; print <- u64.from(lod.impostor.grid); print <- " x "; print <- u64.from(lod.impostor.grid); print <- " frames of ";
    print <- u64.from(lod.impostor.frameSize); print <- " px, "; print <- lod.impostor.textureBytes / 1024u64; print <- " KiB of textures, 2 triangles; porosity ";
    print <- lod.impostor.porosity; print <- (if lod.impostor.hashed { " (alpha hashed)\n" } else { " (alpha cut)\n" });
  }
}

// ---- Targets ----

struct Rig {
  out Texture;
  depth Texture;
  shotBuffer Buffer;
  queries QuerySet;
  resolved Buffer;
  stamps Buffer;
}

fn makeRig(device &mut Device) Rig {
  let outDesc = new TextureDescriptor(W, H, TEXTURE_FORMAT_RGBA8_UNORM_SRGB, TEXTURE_USAGE_RENDER_ATTACHMENT | TEXTURE_USAGE_COPY_SRC);
  let depthDesc = new TextureDescriptor(W, H, TEXTURE_FORMAT_DEPTH32_FLOAT, TEXTURE_USAGE_RENDER_ATTACHMENT | TEXTURE_USAGE_TEXTURE_BINDING);
  var out = device.createTexture(&outDesc);
  var depth = device.createTexture(&depthDesc);
  var shotBuffer = device.createBuffer(u64.from(W) * u64.from(H) * 4u64, BUFFER_USAGE_MAP_READ | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
  var queries = device.createQuerySet(QUERY_TYPE_TIMESTAMP, 2u32);
  var resolved = device.createBuffer(256u64, BUFFER_USAGE_QUERY_RESOLVE | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_SRC);
  var stamps = device.createBuffer(16u64, BUFFER_USAGE_MAP_READ | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
  new Rig(out, depth, shotBuffer, queries, resolved, stamps)
}

// The sun of every picture: a late-afternoon sun, the sky's ambient
fn sunLight() Light {
  Light.directional(new Vec3(-0.55, -0.62, -0.45), new Color(3.2, 2.9, 2.4, 1.), new Color(0.32, 0.38, 0.5, 1.))
}

// A picture of what the scene and the draw list hold, as an Image
fn shoot(device &mut Device, renderer &mut Renderer, rig &Rig, camera &Camera, light &Light, list &DrawList) Image {
  var encoder = device.createCommandEncoder();
  renderer.render(device, &mut encoder, &rig.out, &rig.depth, camera, light, list);
  encoder.copyTextureToBuffer(&rig.out, &rig.shotBuffer);
  device.queue.submit(encoder.finish());
  device.endFrame();
  device.waitIdle();
  Image.fromTexels(rig.shotBuffer.mappedRange(), i32.from(W), i32.from(H), false)
}

// The part of 'img' 'w' by 'h' about (cx, cy)
fn crop(img &Image, cx i32, cy i32, w i32, h i32) Image {
  var out = new Image(w, h, 3, List[u8].withCapacity(usize.from(w * h * 3)));
  var y = 0;
  while y < h {
    var x = 0;
    while x < w {
      var sx = cx - w / 2 + x;
      var sy = cy - h / 2 + y;
      if sx < 0 { sx = 0; }
      if sy < 0 { sy = 0; }
      if sx >= img.width { sx = img.width - 1; }
      if sy >= img.height { sy = img.height - 1; }
      out.pixels.push(img.at(sx, sy, 0));
      out.pixels.push(img.at(sx, sy, 1));
      out.pixels.push(img.at(sx, sy, 2));
      x = x + 1;
    }
    y = y + 1;
  }
  out
}

fn iabs(v i32) i32 { if v < 0 { -v } else { v } }

// How two pictures of the same size differ over the pixels either covers (background colour 'bg'):
// the share of those pixels whose change is above 24 in any channel, and the mean change
struct Pop {
  share f32;
  mean f32;
  covered i32;
}

fn isBackground(img &Image, x i32, y i32, bg &Array[u8]) bool {
  iabs(i32.from(img.at(x, y, 0)) - i32.from(bg[0])) + iabs(i32.from(img.at(x, y, 1)) - i32.from(bg[1]))
    + iabs(i32.from(img.at(x, y, 2)) - i32.from(bg[2])) <= 8
}

fn popBetween(a &Image, b &Image, bg &Array[u8]) Pop {
  var covered = 0;
  var changed = 0;
  var sum = 0.;
  var y = 0;
  while y < a.height {
    var x = 0;
    while x < a.width {
      if !isBackground(a, x, y, bg) or !isBackground(b, x, y, bg) {
        covered = covered + 1;
        var worst = 0;
        var c = 0;
        while c < 3 {
          let d = iabs(i32.from(a.at(x, y, c)) - i32.from(b.at(x, y, c)));
          sum = sum + f32.from(d);
          if d > worst { worst = d; }
          c = c + 1;
        }
        if worst > 24 { changed = changed + 1; }
      }
      x = x + 1;
    }
    y = y + 1;
  }
  new Pop(if covered > 0 { f32.from(changed) / f32.from(covered) } else { 0. }, if covered > 0 { sum / f32.from(covered * 3) } else { 0. }, covered)
}

// The picture enlarged by whole pixels
fn enlarge(img &Image, factor i32) Image {
  var out = new Image(img.width * factor, img.height * factor, 3, List[u8].withCapacity(usize.from(img.width * img.height * factor * factor * 3)));
  var y = 0;
  while y < img.height * factor {
    var x = 0;
    while x < img.width * factor {
      out.pixels.push(img.at(x / factor, y / factor, 0));
      out.pixels.push(img.at(x / factor, y / factor, 1));
      out.pixels.push(img.at(x / factor, y / factor, 2));
      x = x + 1;
    }
    y = y + 1;
  }
  out
}

// The picture blurred by a box of (2 r + 1) pixels each way, edges clamped (a floating point image, 3 channels)
fn boxBlur(img &Image, r i32) List[f32] {
  let w = img.width;
  let h = img.height;
  var tmp = List[f32].withCapacity(usize.from(w * h * 3));
  var out = List[f32].withCapacity(usize.from(w * h * 3));
  var i = 0;
  while i < w * h * 3 { tmp.push(0.); out.push(0.); i = i + 1; }
  var y = 0;
  while y < h {
    var x = 0;
    while x < w {
      var c = 0;
      while c < 3 {
        var sum = 0.;
        var k = -r;
        while k <= r {
          var sx = x + k;
          if sx < 0 { sx = 0; }
          if sx >= w { sx = w - 1; }
          sum = sum + f32.from(img.at(sx, y, c));
          k = k + 1;
        }
        tmp.set(usize.from((y * w + x) * 3 + c), sum / f32.from(2 * r + 1));
        c = c + 1;
      }
      x = x + 1;
    }
    y = y + 1;
  }
  y = 0;
  while y < h {
    var x = 0;
    while x < w {
      var c = 0;
      while c < 3 {
        var sum = 0.;
        var k = -r;
        while k <= r {
          var sy = y + k;
          if sy < 0 { sy = 0; }
          if sy >= h { sy = h - 1; }
          sum = sum + *tmp[usize.from((sy * w + x) * 3 + c)];
          k = k + 1;
        }
        out.set(usize.from((y * w + x) * 3 + c), sum / f32.from(2 * r + 1));
        c = c + 1;
      }
      x = x + 1;
    }
    y = y + 1;
  }
  out
}

// How much the two pictures differ in tone, seen through a blur of radius r: the mean change of the blurred
// pixels over those within r of either picture's subject, 0 to 255
fn toneChange(a &Image, b &Image, bg &Array[u8], r i32) f32 {
  let ba = boxBlur(a, r);
  let bb = boxBlur(b, r);
  var sum = 0.;
  var n = 0;
  var y = 0;
  while y < a.height {
    var x = 0;
    while x < a.width {
      var near = false;
      var dy = -r;
      while dy <= r and !near {
        var dx = -r;
        while dx <= r and !near {
          let sx = x + dx;
          let sy = y + dy;
          if sx >= 0 and sx < a.width and sy >= 0 and sy < a.height {
            if !isBackground(a, sx, sy, bg) or !isBackground(b, sx, sy, bg) { near = true; }
          }
          dx = dx + 1;
        }
        dy = dy + 1;
      }
      if near {
        var c = 0;
        while c < 3 {
          let i = usize.from((y * a.width + x) * 3 + c);
          sum = sum + (if *ba[i] > *bb[i] { *ba[i] - *bb[i] } else { *bb[i] - *ba[i] });
          c = c + 1;
        }
        n = n + 1;
      }
      x = x + 1;
    }
    y = y + 1;
  }
  if n > 0 { sum / f32.from(n * 3) } else { 0. }
}

// The difference of two pictures, amplified 4 times
fn differenceImage(a &Image, b &Image) Image {
  var out = new Image(a.width, a.height, 3, List[u8].withCapacity(usize.from(a.width * a.height * 3)));
  var y = 0;
  while y < a.height {
    var x = 0;
    while x < a.width {
      var c = 0;
      while c < 3 {
        var d = iabs(i32.from(a.at(x, y, c)) - i32.from(b.at(x, y, c))) * 4;
        if d > 255 { d = 255; }
        out.pixels.push(u8.from(d));
        c = c + 1;
      }
      x = x + 1;
    }
    y = y + 1;
  }
  out
}

fn save(folder &str, name &str, img &Image) {
  var path = String.from(folder);
  path <- "/";
  path <- name;
  path <- ".bmp";
  img.save(&filepath.Path.from(path.view()));
}

fn encodeSrgb(l f32) f32 {
  if l <= 0.0031308 { return l * 12.92; }
  1.055 * libc.powf(l, 1. / 2.4) - 0.055
}

// ---- A subject in the renderer ----

struct Subject {
  name String;
  parts List[BakePart];
  lod AutoLod;
  meshChains List[LodChain];          // the same chains without the impostor (and the other parts' hidden level)
  materials List[MaterialHandle];     // the renderer's, one a part
  center Vec3;
  radius f32;
  bakeMilliseconds f64;
}

fn addSubject(device &mut Device, renderer &mut Renderer, name &str, parts List[BakePart], pipe &ImpostorPipeline,
    baker &mut ImpostorBaker, settings &AutoLodSettings) Subject {
  let t0 = sdl.GetPerformanceCounter();
  let lod = autoLod(device, renderer, pipe, baker, &parts, settings);
  let t1 = sdl.GetPerformanceCounter();
  var materials = List[MaterialHandle].empty();
  var meshChains = List[LodChain].empty();
  var p = 0usize;
  while p < parts.len() {
    let m = parts[p].material;
    materials.push(renderer.addMaterial(device, &m));
    let full = lod.chains[p];
    var mc = LodChain.empty(settings.lods.hysteresis);
    var k = 0usize;
    let keep = if lod.hasImpostor { full.levels.len() - 1usize } else { full.levels.len() };
    while k < keep {
      mc.add(*full.levels[k], *full.minSizes[k]);
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    meshChains.push(mc);
    p = p + 1usize;
  }
  let center = lod.center;
  let radius = lod.radius;
  new Subject(String.from(name), parts, lod, meshChains, materials, center, radius, seconds(t0, t1) * 1000d)
}

// How a copy is planted: no levels, the mesh levels, or the mesh levels and the impostor
const PLANT_FLAT = 0;
const PLANT_MESHES = 1;
const PLANT_FULL = 2;

fn plant(renderer &mut Renderer, s &Subject, model Mat4, mode i32, range f32) {
  var p = 0usize;
  while p < s.lod.chains.len() {
    let full = s.lod.chains[p];
    let meshes = s.meshChains[p];
    let item = renderer.addSceneItem(*full.levels[0usize], *s.materials[p], model, new Color(1., 1., 1., 1.));
    if mode == PLANT_MESHES { renderer.setSceneLod(item, meshes); }
    if mode == PLANT_FULL { renderer.setSceneLod(item, full); }
    if range > 0. { renderer.setSceneRange(item, 0., range, range * 0.08); }
    p = p + 1usize;
  }
}

// How far the camera must stand for the whole subject to be 'px' pixels across in a 1080-pixel-high picture
fn distanceForSize(radius f32, px f32, fov f32) f32 {
  radius / (px / f32.from(H) * libc.tanf(fov * 0.5))
}

// The level of the chain that a size selects, from a fresh start at level 0
fn levelAtSize(chain &LodChain, size f32) usize {
  selectLod(chain, size, 0usize)
}

// The subject drawn alone by DrawList, with chain level 'levels[part]' of each part (the impostor with its own material)
fn drawLevels(device &mut Device, renderer &mut Renderer, rig &Rig, s &Subject, levels &List[usize], camera &Camera,
    light &Light, ground MeshHandle, groundMaterial MaterialHandle, model Mat4) Image {
  renderer.clearScene();
  var list = DrawList.empty();
  var p = 0usize;
  while p < s.lod.chains.len() {
    let level = *levels[p];
    let chain = s.lod.chains[p];
    let own = chain.materialOf(level);
    let material = if own.isNone() { *s.materials[p] } else { own };
    list.add(*chain.levels[level], material, model);
    p = p + 1usize;
  }
  shoot(device, renderer, rig, camera, light, &list)
}

// ---- The shots ----

fn shotsFor(device &mut Device, renderer &mut Renderer, rig &Rig, s &Subject, folder &str, settings &AutoLodSettings) {
  let light = sunLight();
  let groundMesh = renderer.addMesh(device, &Mesh.plane(1, 1.));
  let groundMaterial = renderer.addMaterial(device, &Material.plain(new Color(0.16, 0.22, 0.08, 1.)));
  var camera = Camera.make();
  camera.fov = radians(40.);
  camera.near = 0.5;
  camera.far = 5000.;
  let bg = new Color(0.45, 0.58, 0.75, 1.);
  camera.background = bg;
  // the background in sRGB bytes: the target encodes it
  let bgBytes = [u8.from(255. * encodeSrgb(bg.red) + 0.5), u8.from(255. * encodeSrgb(bg.green) + 0.5), u8.from(255. * encodeSrgb(bg.blue) + 0.5)];
  let dir = new Vec3(0.55, 0.22, 0.8).normalize();
  let lookAt = new Vec3(0., s.center.y, 0.);
  let modelAt = Mat4.identity();
  let sizes = settings.lods.levels;

  // At each switch: just above the size and just below it, the finer level and the coarser, each drawn alone
  var k = 1u32;
  while k <= sizes {
    // switch k: from the level whose threshold it is (k - 1, from the sizes' list) to the next; the last is to the impostor
    let hasNext = if k < sizes { true } else { s.lod.hasImpostor };
    if hasNext {
      let threshold = settings.lods.switchSize(k - 1u32);
      var finerLevels = List[usize].empty();
      var coarserLevels = List[usize].empty();
      var p = 0usize;
      while p < s.lod.chains.len() {
        // each part's own size is the object's times its radius over the object's; the levels either side of
        // the switch (clear of the chain's hysteresis band)
        let chain = s.lod.chains[p];
        let scale = s.lod.sets[p].radius / s.radius;
        finerLevels.push(levelAtSize(chain, threshold * 1.25 * scale));
        coarserLevels.push(levelAtSize(chain, threshold * 0.7 * scale));
        p = p + 1usize;
      }
      // both are drawn where the scene would make the change, going away: at 85% of the threshold (the hysteresis)
      let distance = distanceForSize(s.radius, threshold * (1. - settings.lods.hysteresis), camera.fov);
      camera.lookAt(lookAt + dir * distance, lookAt, new Vec3(0., 1., 0.));
      let finer = drawLevels(device, renderer, rig, s, &finerLevels, &camera, &light, groundMesh, groundMaterial, modelAt);
      let coarser = drawLevels(device, renderer, rig, s, &coarserLevels, &camera, &light, groundMesh, groundMaterial, modelAt);
      // a crop of 1.5 times the object's size, shown enlarged by whole pixels to about 360
      let box = if i32.from(threshold * 1.5) > 40 { i32.from(threshold * 1.5) } else { 40 };
      let sx = i32.from(W) / 2;
      let sy = i32.from(H) / 2;
      let cropA = crop(&finer, sx, sy, box, box);
      let cropB = crop(&coarser, sx, sy, box, box);
      let pop = popBetween(&cropA, &cropB, &bgBytes);
      let tone = toneChange(&cropA, &cropB, &bgBytes, 4);
      let factor = if 360 / box > 1 { 360 / box } else { 1 };
      var tag = String.from(s.name.view());
      tag <- "-switch"; tag.appendInt(i64.from(k));
      var nameA = tag.copy(); nameA <- "-finer";
      var nameB = tag.copy(); nameB <- "-coarser";
      var nameD = tag.copy(); nameD <- "-difference";
      save(folder, nameA.view(), &enlarge(&cropA, factor));
      save(folder, nameB.view(), &enlarge(&cropB, factor));
      save(folder, nameD.view(), &enlarge(&differenceImage(&cropA, &cropB), factor));
      printStr(s.name.view()); print <- " switch "; print <- u64.from(k); print <- " at "; print <- threshold; print <- " px ("; print <- distance;
      print <- " m): levels ";
      var q = 0usize;
      while q < finerLevels.len() {
        print <- u64.from(*finerLevels[q]); print <- ">"; print <- u64.from(*coarserLevels[q]); print <- " ";
        q = q + 1usize;
      }
      print <- "; pop: "; print <- pop.share * 100.; print <- "% of the "; print <- u64.from(pop.covered);
      print <- " pixels it covers change by more than 24/255, mean change "; print <- pop.mean; print <- "/255; seen through a blur of 9 pixels the mean tone change is ";
      print <- tone; print <- "/255\n";
    }
    k = k + 1u32;
  }

  // Through the scene at distances, levels chosen by size
  let distances = [10., 30., 100., 300., 1000., 2000.];
  var d = 0usize;
  while d < 6usize {
    renderer.clearScene();
    renderer.vis.settings = new VisibilitySettings();
    renderer.vis.settings.fadeSeconds = 0.0001;
    renderer.addSceneItem(groundMesh, groundMaterial, Mat4.fromTrs(new Vec3(0., 0., 0.), Quat.identity(), new Vec3(3000., 1., 3000.)),
      new Color(1., 1., 1., 1.));
    plant(renderer, s, modelAt, PLANT_FULL, 0.);
    let dist = distances[d];
    camera.lookAt(lookAt + dir * dist, lookAt, new Vec3(0., 1., 0.));
    let empty = DrawList.empty();
    shoot(device, renderer, rig, &camera, &light, &empty);
    let img = shoot(device, renderer, rig, &camera, &light, &empty);
    let size = camera.projectedSize(lookAt, s.radius, f32.from(H));
    let box = if dist <= 30. { 540 } elif dist <= 300. { 360 } else { 120 };
    let cropped = enlarge(&crop(&img, i32.from(W) / 2, i32.from(H) / 2, box, box), if box < 200 { 3 } else { 1 });
    var name = String.from(s.name.view());
    name <- "-at"; name.appendInt(i64.from(i32.from(dist)));
    save(folder, name.view(), &cropped);
    printStr(s.name.view()); print <- " at "; print <- dist; print <- " m: "; print <- size; print <- " px across, ";
    print <- u64.from(renderer.triangles); print <- " triangles drawn (ground included), "; print <- u64.from(renderer.drawCalls); print <- " draws\n";
    d = d + 1usize;
  }
  renderer.clearScene();
}

// ---- The bench ----

fn scatter(n u32) f32 {
  var x = n * 747796405u32 + 2891336453u32;
  x = ((x >> ((x >> 28u32) + 4u32)) ^ x) * 277803737u32;
  x = (x >> 22u32) ^ x;
  f32.from(x & 0xFFFFu32) / 65535.
}

const FRAMES = 40u32;

struct Cost {
  gpu f64;
  cpu f64;
}

fn timeFrames(device &mut Device, renderer &mut Renderer, rig &Rig, camera &Camera, light &Light) Cost {
  let empty = DrawList.empty();
  var gpuTime = 0d;
  var cpuTime = 0d;
  var counted = 0u32;
  var f = 0u32;
  while f < FRAMES {
    let t0 = sdl.GetPerformanceCounter();
    var encoder = device.createCommandEncoder();
    encoder.writeTimestamp(&rig.queries, 0u32);
    renderer.render(device, &mut encoder, &rig.out, &rig.depth, camera, light, &empty);
    encoder.writeTimestamp(&rig.queries, 1u32);
    encoder.resolveQuerySet(&rig.queries, 0u32, 2u32, &rig.resolved, 0u64);
    encoder.copyBufferToBuffer(&rig.resolved, 0u64, &rig.stamps, 0u64, 16u64);
    device.queue.submit(encoder.finish());
    let t1 = sdl.GetPerformanceCounter();
    device.endFrame();
    device.waitIdle();
    if f >= 8u32 {
      let ticks = rig.stamps.mappedRange() as *u64;
      gpuTime = gpuTime + f64.from(*(ticks + 1usize) - *ticks) * f64.from(device.timestampPeriod) * 1.0e-6d;
      cpuTime = cpuTime + seconds(t0, t1) * 1000d;
      counted = counted + 1u32;
    }
    f = f + 1u32;
  }
  new Cost(gpuTime / f64.from(counted), cpuTime / f64.from(counted))
}

fn benchWorld(device &mut Device, renderer &mut Renderer, rig &Rig, subjects &List[Subject], mode i32, folder &str) {
  renderer.clearScene();
  renderer.vis.settings = new VisibilitySettings();
  let groundMesh = renderer.addMesh(device, &Mesh.plane(1, 1.));
  let groundMaterial = renderer.addMaterial(device, &Material.plain(new Color(0.16, 0.22, 0.08, 1.)));
  renderer.addSceneItem(groundMesh, groundMaterial, Mat4.fromTrs(new Vec3(0., 0., 0.), Quat.identity(), new Vec3(4200., 1., 4200.)),
    new Color(1., 1., 1., 1.));
  // 6,000 maples (three kinds), 1,500 rocks (two), 150 houses
  var placed = 0u32;
  var n = 0u32;
  while placed < 7650u32 {
    let x = (scatter(n * 5u32) - 0.5) * 4000.;
    let z = (scatter(n * 5u32 + 1u32) - 0.5) * 4000.;
    let yaw = scatter(n * 5u32 + 2u32) * 6.2831853;
    let sc = 0.75 + scatter(n * 5u32 + 3u32) * 0.6;
    n = n + 1u32;
    // keep a clearing where the camera stands (a hundred metres round it)
    if x * x + (z - 1900.) * (z - 1900.) < 10000. { continue; }
    var kind = 0usize;
    if placed < 6000u32 { kind = usize.from(placed % 3u32); }
    elif placed < 7500u32 { kind = 3usize + usize.from(placed % 2u32); }
    else { kind = 5usize; }
    let model = Mat4.fromTrs(new Vec3(x, 0., z), Quat.angleAxis(yaw, new Vec3(0., 1., 0.)), new Vec3(sc, sc, sc));
    plant(renderer, subjects[kind], model, mode, 2500.);
    placed = placed + 1u32;
  }
  let light = sunLight();
  var camera = Camera.make();
  camera.fov = radians(60.);
  camera.near = 0.3;
  camera.far = 3200.;
  camera.background = new Color(0.45, 0.58, 0.75, 1.);
  var v = 0;
  while v < 2 {
    if v == 0 {
      camera.lookAt(new Vec3(0., 2., 1900.), new Vec3(0., 12., 0.), new Vec3(0., 1., 0.));
    } else {
      camera.lookAt(new Vec3(0., 120., 2100.), new Vec3(0., 0., 300.), new Vec3(0., 1., 0.));
    }
    let cost = timeFrames(device, renderer, rig, &camera, &light);
    printStr(if mode == PLANT_FLAT { "    levels off          " } elif mode == PLANT_MESHES { "    mesh levels         " } else { "    mesh levels + card  " });
    printStr(if v == 0 { "eye level: " } else { "from 120 m: " });
    print <- "GPU "; print <- cost.gpu; print <- " ms, CPU "; print <- cost.cpu; print <- " ms; ";
    print <- u64.from(renderer.vis.stats.drawn); print <- " items drawn of "; print <- u64.from(renderer.vis.stats.items); print <- ", ";
    print <- renderer.triangles; print <- " triangles, "; print <- u64.from(renderer.drawCalls); print <- " draws, ";
    print <- u64.from(renderer.vis.stats.lodSwitches); print <- " switches, "; print <- u64.from(renderer.vis.stats.fading); print <- " fading\n";
    if folder.len() > 0usize {
      let empty = DrawList.empty();
      let img = shoot(device, renderer, rig, &camera, &light, &empty);
      var name = String.from("forest-");
      name <- if mode == PLANT_FLAT { "flat" } elif mode == PLANT_MESHES { "meshes" } else { "full" };
      name <- if v == 0 { "-eye" } else { "-high" };
      save(folder, name.view(), &img);
    }
    v = v + 1;
  }
  renderer.clearScene();
}

fn main(argc i32, argv **u8) i32 {
  var mode = 0;
  var folder = String.from("");
  var a = 1;
  while a < argc {
    let arg = *(argv + usize.from(a));
    if cstrEquals(arg, "--report") { mode = 1; }
    elif cstrEquals(arg, "--bench") { mode = 3; }
    elif (cstrEquals(arg, "--shots") or cstrEquals(arg, "--benchshots")) and a + 1 < argc {
      mode = if cstrEquals(arg, "--shots") { 2 } else { 4 };
      let s = *(argv + usize.from(a + 1));
      var i = 0usize;
      while *(s + i) != 0u8 {
        folder.appendByte(*(s + i));
        i = i + 1usize;
      }
      a = a + 1;
    } else {
      print <- "Usage: --report | --shots FOLDER | --bench | --benchshots FOLDER\n";
      return 2;
    }
    a = a + 1;
  }
  if mode == 0 {
    print <- "Usage: --report | --shots FOLDER | --bench | --benchshots FOLDER\n";
    return 2;
  }
  var instance = Instance.create("autolod example");
  var none = Surface.none();
  var preference = POWER_PREFERENCE_HIGH_PERFORMANCE;
  let env = libc.getenv("GPU_POWER_PREFERENCE");
  if (env as usize) != 0usize {
    if libc.strcmp(cstr.fromPtr(env), "low-power") == 0i32 { preference = POWER_PREFERENCE_LOW_POWER; }
  }
  var adapter = instance.requestAdapter(&none, preference);
  if !adapter.isValid() {
    print <- "No GPU\n";
    return 1i32;
  }
  print <- "Adapter: "; printStr(adapter.name.view()); print <- "\n";
  var device = adapter.requestDevice();
  let rig = makeRig(&mut device);
  var renderer = Renderer.create(&mut device, TEXTURE_FORMAT_RGBA8_UNORM_SRGB, TEXTURE_FORMAT_DEPTH32_FLOAT);
  if !renderer.isValid() or !rig.queries.isValid() {
    print <- "The renderer or the timestamps could not be made\n";
    return 1i32;
  }
  var settings = new AutoLodSettings();
  settings.lods.measure = mode == 1;
  var baker = ImpostorBaker.create(&mut device, settings.impostor.frameSize);
  let pipe = makeImpostorPipeline(&mut renderer, &mut device);
  if !baker.isValid() or !pipe.isValid(&renderer) {
    print <- "The baker or the impostor pipeline could not be made\n";
    return 1i32;
  }
  var subjects = List[Subject].empty();
  // three maples (seeds), two rocks, a house: the subjects of the bench's world
  subjects.push(addSubject(&mut device, &mut renderer, "maple", mapleParts(3u32, 12.), &pipe, &mut baker, &settings));
  if mode == 3 or mode == 4 {
    subjects.push(addSubject(&mut device, &mut renderer, "maple2", mapleParts(4u32, 10.), &pipe, &mut baker, &settings));
    subjects.push(addSubject(&mut device, &mut renderer, "maple3", mapleParts(9u32, 14.), &pipe, &mut baker, &settings));
    subjects.push(addSubject(&mut device, &mut renderer, "rock", rockParts(5u32), &pipe, &mut baker, &settings));
    subjects.push(addSubject(&mut device, &mut renderer, "rock2", rockParts(8u32), &pipe, &mut baker, &settings));
    subjects.push(addSubject(&mut device, &mut renderer, "house", houseParts(), &pipe, &mut baker, &settings));
  } else {
    subjects.push(addSubject(&mut device, &mut renderer, "rock", rockParts(5u32), &pipe, &mut baker, &settings));
    subjects.push(addSubject(&mut device, &mut renderer, "house", houseParts(), &pipe, &mut baker, &settings));
  }
  var s = 0usize;
  while s < subjects.len() {
    print <- subjects[s].name.view(); print <- ": levels and impostor made in "; print <- subjects[s].bakeMilliseconds; print <- " ms\n";
    s = s + 1usize;
  }
  if mode == 1 or mode == 2 {
    s = 0usize;
    while s < subjects.len() {
      reportOne(subjects[s].name.view(), &subjects[s].parts, &subjects[s].lod, &settings);
      s = s + 1usize;
    }
  }
  if mode == 2 {
    s = 0usize;
    while s < subjects.len() {
      shotsFor(&mut device, &mut renderer, &rig, subjects[s], folder.view(), &settings);
      s = s + 1usize;
    }
  }
  if mode == 3 or mode == 4 {
    print <- "A world of 6,000 maples (2 parts each), 1,500 rocks and 150 houses (4 parts each) over 4 km by 4 km, 2.5 km range:\n";
    let shotFolder = if mode == 4 { folder.view() } else { "" };
    benchWorld(&mut device, &mut renderer, &rig, &subjects, PLANT_FLAT, shotFolder);
    benchWorld(&mut device, &mut renderer, &rig, &subjects, PLANT_MESHES, shotFolder);
    benchWorld(&mut device, &mut renderer, &rig, &subjects, PLANT_FULL, shotFolder);
    print <- "  with cascaded shadows (medium):\n";
    let shadows = ShadowSettings.medium();
    renderer.setShadows(&mut device, &shadows);
    benchWorld(&mut device, &mut renderer, &rig, &subjects, PLANT_FLAT, "");
    benchWorld(&mut device, &mut renderer, &rig, &subjects, PLANT_MESHES, "");
    benchWorld(&mut device, &mut renderer, &rig, &subjects, PLANT_FULL, "");
  }
  device.waitIdle();
  print <- "Validation messages: "; print <- u64.from(validationMessages()); print <- "\n";
  0i32
}
